      "title": "Note: MiniMax H3",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 Image to Video (vlo)\n\n[MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) generates video with **native stereo audio** \u2014 voice, sound effects and music are modelled jointly in a single forward pass, not layered on afterward.\n\n## About this workflow\n\nThe `MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo` node covers two tasks with the same checkpoint:\n\n- **t2va** (text to video + audio) when neither keyframe is provided\n- **fl2va** (first / last frame) when either keyframe is provided\n\nBoth **Start frame** and **End frame** are optional in vlo: leave both empty for a pure text-to-video generation, or provide either one on its own.\n\n**Key inputs**\n\n- **Start frame / End frame**: optional keyframes; the model generates the motion between them. Each is stretched to the generation canvas first, so both keyframes are treated identically.\n- **Prompt**: describe the shots, motion, and the accompanying audio (dialogue, SFX, music) in one block\n- **Width / Height**: driven by vlo's resolution and aspect-ratio controls. H3's native canvas is a 768px short edge, capped at 768x1344 pixels, rounded to a multiple of 32\n- **Length**: frame count at 24fps on the model's 17k+5 grid, so the vlo slider runs 22 frames (~0.9s) to 600 frames (25s) in steps of 17"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MiniMax H3 Image to Video (vlo)\n\n[MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) generates video with **native stereo audio** \u2014 voice, sound effects and music are modelled jointly in a single forward pass, not layered on afterward.\n\n## About this workflow\n\nThe `MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo` node covers two tasks with the same checkpoint:\n\n- **t2va** (text to video + audio) when neither keyframe is provided\n- **fl2va** (first / last frame) when either keyframe is provided\n\nBoth **Start frame** and **End frame** are optional in vlo: leave both empty for a pure text-to-video generation, or provide either one on its own.\n\n**Key inputs**\n\n- **Start frame / End frame**: optional keyframes; the model generates the motion between them. Each is stretched to the generation canvas first, so both keyframes are treated identically.\n- **Prompt**: describe the shots, motion, and the accompanying audio (dialogue, SFX, music) in one block\n- **Width / Height**: driven by vlo's resolution and aspect-ratio controls. H3's native canvas is a 768px short edge, capped at 768x1344 pixels, rounded to a multiple of 32\n- **Length**: frame count at 24fps on the model's 17k+5 grid, so the vlo slider runs 22 frames (~0.9s) to 600 frames (25s) in steps of 17"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
